 ## shell.css
 
-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width (superseded by §viewport-media-query)
 - Since: 2026-09-15
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
 - Reason: the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen. Viewport queries picked the
   two-column layout inside a narrow pane and clipped the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14).
+
+### §viewport-media-query — the shell's layout step uses a viewport media query
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport
+- Decision: the shell's layout step is `@media (min-width: 720px)`; `container-type` is removed from `.shell`.
+- Reason: team decision in the sync of 2026-10-23 to drop container queries (not widely used or understood on the team).
+- Known risk: the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen; on a wide viewport the
+  two-column layout will apply inside a narrow pane and can clip the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14). Accepted by the
+  requester; not verified in a split pane.
